00:08:04.580 --> 00:08:09.320
<b></b>Sawaragi Shiho

00:08:04.930 --> 00:08:07.560
Basically, if we promise 
to play the game like that,

00:08:05.280 --> 00:08:10.510
<b></b>Katagiri Yuichi

00:08:06.990 --> 00:08:10.510
<b></b>Shibe Makoto

00:08:06.990 --> 00:08:10.510
<b></b>Kokorogi Yutori

00:08:07.560 --> 00:08:10.510
it's essentially the same 
as signing our votes.

00:08:10.510 --> 00:08:12.380
<b></b>Bad-Mouth
 1st Shibe -> yes
 Shiho -> yes
 Yutori -> yes
 Yuichi -> no
 Tenji -> yes

00:08:10.510 --> 00:08:13.800
The traitor won't be able 
to betray us any more!

00:08:13.800 --> 00:08:17.350
I get it! That's why we don't need 
to say who the traitor is.

00:08:17.840 --> 00:08:21.100
This way, we'd have to 
move one space at a time.

00:08:21.100 --> 00:08:24.570
If we follow each other in order 
and share our own secrets,

00:08:24.570 --> 00:08:27.730
it should be possible to catch 
up to the same space.

00:08:27.730 --> 00:08:29.980
Possible, you say...

00:08:29.980 --> 00:08:33.070
Yeah. It's not a perfect strategy.

00:08:33.070 --> 00:08:35.030
But at least...

00:08:35.670 --> 00:08:38.660
we could stop trying to hurt each other.

00:08:39.320 --> 00:08:43.810
I know we've all been through a lot, but can
 we try to work together one more time?

00:08:43.810 --> 00:08:46.380
Our debt shouldn't increase 
from here on out.

00:08:46.970 --> 00:08:50.960
Wouldn't it suck if our 
friendship ended like this?

00:08:50.960 --> 00:08:53.260
When you put it that way, Yuichi...

00:08:53.260 --> 00:08:54.800
I'm against it!

00:08:54.800 --> 00:08:58.680
Why, Tenji? Everyone else is on board.

00:08:58.680 --> 00:09:03.520
Or... is there some reason why 
it wouldn't work out for you?

00:09:05.480 --> 00:09:09.980
Yuichi, do you really know 
who the traitor is?

00:09:09.980 --> 00:09:13.240
O-Of course I do. 
Why are you so intent on asking?

00:09:13.240 --> 00:09:15.110
Then spit it out!

00:09:15.910 --> 00:09:19.890
That way everyone can concentrate 
their votes on the traitor

00:09:19.890 --> 00:09:21.450
and make them finish first.

00:09:21.450 --> 00:09:23.540
Isn't that the best strategy?

00:09:23.540 --> 00:09:26.870
B-But then, I know he's the traitor,

00:09:26.870 --> 00:09:28.920
but he'll be sent to the third game alone.

00:09:28.920 --> 00:09:29.910
That's too cruel—

00:09:29.910 --> 00:09:31.170
Don't be dense!

00:09:31.170 --> 00:09:35.030
<b>Katagiri</b>

00:09:32.090 --> 00:09:37.550
Yuichi, at this point, I think 
it's stupid to trust anyone.

00:09:37.960 --> 00:09:40.290
We're getting into the final rounds.

00:09:40.290 --> 00:09:44.330
If we waste a valuable period on
 this strategy and it doesn't work,

00:09:44.330 --> 00:09:47.140
I'm gonna make you tell us who the traitor is.

00:09:47.140 --> 00:09:48.410
Y-Yeah.

00:09:48.410 --> 00:09:50.050
And!

00:09:50.050 --> 00:09:52.790
If you identify the traitor 
without any kind of proof,

00:09:52.790 --> 00:09:55.090
I'm never listening to you again.

00:09:55.090 --> 00:09:56.510
Is that all right with you?!

00:09:58.710 --> 00:10:00.370
That's fine with me.

00:10:00.370 --> 00:10:01.450
Is it?

00:10:02.690 --> 00:10:03.950
Okay.

00:10:03.950 --> 00:10:05.830
<b>Eighth Period</b>

00:10:06.140 --> 00:10:09.040
Did everyone bad-mouth yourselves? 
Except Shibe, since he's in first.

00:10:09.040 --> 00:10:10.000
Yeah.

00:10:10.000 --> 00:10:11.140
Of course.

00:10:12.880 --> 00:10:13.770
Good.

00:10:13.770 --> 00:10:16.050
There should be exactly 
four bad-mouth cards.

00:10:16.050 --> 00:10:17.750
Even if there aren't that many,

00:10:17.750 --> 00:10:20.180
we should know right 
away who didn't write one.

00:10:20.180 --> 00:10:23.260
Let's see, this time there are...

00:10:24.890 --> 00:10:27.730
ten cards in total!

00:10:29.480 --> 00:10:31.560
Ten... cards?

00:10:34.410 --> 00:10:37.010
There were ten cards in the box!

00:10:37.010 --> 00:10:38.380
Ten cards?

00:10:38.380 --> 00:10:42.620
<i>Sorry, Yuichi. There were holes 
in your plan from the start.</i>

00:10:42.620 --> 00:10:46.060
I'm honestly disappointed in you, Yuichi.

00:10:46.060 --> 00:10:48.960
I was surprised when you said 
you had a strategy,

00:10:48.960 --> 00:10:51.430
but your plan was <i>so</i> weak!

00:10:51.430 --> 00:10:57.190
Sure, if you could only write one card 
each time, your strategy would work,

00:10:53.590 --> 00:10:59.170
<b>- You can write as many things as you want about each person</b>

00:10:57.190 --> 00:10:59.190
but you have to remember the rules.

00:10:59.190 --> 00:11:03.350
One of you probably put in 
a whole lot of cards.

00:11:03.350 --> 00:11:06.620
Yuichi-kun, you're pretty dumb, aren't you?

00:11:07.600 --> 00:11:09.230
I saw this coming,

00:11:09.840 --> 00:11:12.410
but you said you were confident,

00:11:12.410 --> 00:11:14.530
so I thought you had 
something up your sleeve.

00:11:14.530 --> 00:11:16.880
No, I had no idea this would happen!

00:11:16.880 --> 00:11:20.140
Fine. No turning back now. You promised.

00:11:20.140 --> 00:11:24.180
<i>This will be our final duel, Yuichi!</i>

00:11:24.180 --> 00:11:26.830
Which one of us is the traitor?

00:11:27.820 --> 00:11:29.040
It's...

00:11:29.280 --> 00:11:31.990
<i>If you say my name, you'll win.</i>

00:11:31.990 --> 00:11:36.830
<i>But if you say nothing, I'll be 
the victor of Bad-Mouth Sugoroku!</i>

00:11:37.340 --> 00:11:41.080
I-I'm sorry. I was bluffing.

00:11:41.080 --> 00:11:43.980
I don't even know if 
there's a traitor or not.

00:11:45.720 --> 00:11:47.510
Let's go, Shiho-chan.

00:11:47.510 --> 00:11:51.270
But Yuichi did all of that to help us...

00:11:51.270 --> 00:11:53.090
You always say things like that!

00:11:53.090 --> 00:11:55.550
That's why you keep getting 
hurt, over and over!

00:11:55.550 --> 00:11:57.070
I-I'm sorry.

00:11:57.480 --> 00:11:59.740
You have to accept it.

00:12:00.270 --> 00:12:05.090
Our friendship is already totally ruined!

00:12:05.780 --> 00:12:12.410
<b></b>Mikasa Tenji

00:12:06.170 --> 00:12:11.030
If we stay in denial, we're just 
going to keep getting beaten.

00:12:12.420 --> 00:12:15.920
Don't worry, though. I'll keep 
protecting you, no matter what.

00:12:15.920 --> 00:12:17.460
Come with me.

00:12:19.510 --> 00:12:20.530
Yeah.

00:12:21.560 --> 00:12:23.180
<i>I've won!</i>

00:12:24.280 --> 00:12:28.060
<i>Now there's no one standing in my way.</i>

00:12:28.740 --> 00:12:34.270
<i>It's been two years since you stole 
what was most precious to me.</i>

00:12:34.270 --> 00:12:37.240
<i>Finally. Finally.</i>

00:12:37.240 --> 00:12:43.170
<i>I've been waiting for this chance 
for a long, </i>long<i> time.</i>

00:12:44.320 --> 00:12:48.910
<i>I've waited so long for vengeance...</i>

00:12:49.450 --> 00:12:55.870
<i>Now, all I have to do is set the stage 
to lay you open for everyone to see!</i>

00:12:55.870 --> 00:13:00.260
Senpai, it looks like Group C 
is finished, doesn't it?

00:13:00.260 --> 00:13:02.460
Yes, you might be right.

00:13:02.460 --> 00:13:06.810
<i>The rest of the game horribly slogged on.</i>

00:13:06.340 --> 00:13:15.230
<b>Ninth Period 
Tenth Period 
Eleventh Period 
Twelfth Period 
Thirteenth Period 
Fourteenth Period 
Fifteenth Period 
Sixteenth Period 
Seventeenth Period 
Eighteenth Period</b>

00:13:06.810 --> 00:13:10.080
<i>Nobody spoke to or even 
looked at anyone else.</i>

00:13:10.080 --> 00:13:15.220
<i>The game proceeded as the traitor
 had likely intended.</i>

00:13:15.230 --> 00:13:16.980
<b>Nineteenth Period</b>

00:13:16.980 --> 00:13:21.420
Aw, you're back in first place 
again, Shiho-sama.

00:13:22.440 --> 00:13:25.100
And you're only one space from the goal!

00:13:25.100 --> 00:13:28.150
By the way, to reach the goal 
you have to jump off the edge.

00:13:28.150 --> 00:13:31.540
Don't worry! It's a little scary, 
but you won't die.

00:13:31.540 --> 00:13:36.000
I'm sorry, Shiho-chan! I wasn't 
strong enough to protect you.

00:13:36.710 --> 00:13:41.800
If only I had given up on trusting everyone 
sooner, this wouldn't have happened.

00:13:41.800 --> 00:13:43.760
<i>Come on, let me hear it.</i>

00:13:43.760 --> 00:13:47.550
<i>Tell me how you really feel now that 
you're backed into a corner!</i>

00:13:47.550 --> 00:13:51.260
Aw, this group ended up 
just like the others.

00:13:51.260 --> 00:13:53.380
It was all over too soon.

00:13:53.380 --> 00:13:54.760
That's true.

00:13:54.390 --> 00:14:02.400
<b>Period 19       Spaces </b>Moved<b>      Debt Amount </b>(game 2 only)<b></b>

00:13:54.390 --> 00:14:02.400
<b><b>Shiho</b></b>

00:13:54.390 --> 00:14:02.400
<b><b>Shibe</b></b>

00:13:54.390 --> 00:14:02.400
<b><b>Yuichi</b></b>

00:13:54.390 --> 00:14:02.400
<b><b>Tenji</b></b>

00:13:54.390 --> 00:14:02.400
<b><b>Yutori</b></b>

00:13:54.390 --> 00:14:02.400
<b>59 </b>spaces - <b>100,000 </b>yen

00:13:54.390 --> 00:14:02.400
<b>52 </b>spaces - <b>300,000 </b>yen

00:13:54.390 --> 00:14:02.400
<b>49 </b>spaces - <b>200,000 </b>yen

00:13:54.390 --> 00:14:02.400
<b>44 </b>spaces - <b>400,000 </b>yen

00:13:54.390 --> 00:14:02.400
<b>32 </b>spaces - <b>800,000 </b>yen

00:13:54.390 --> 00:14:02.400
<b>Goal: <b>60 </b>spaces</b>

00:13:54.760 --> 00:13:58.930
<i>At this point, no matter what people 
write, they'll never catch up to Shiho.</i>

00:13:58.930 --> 00:14:02.400
<i>Even if they're all blank, 
she has to move one space.</i>

00:14:02.400 --> 00:14:06.210
<i>Sawaragi Shiho is the single 
confirmed loser of this second game.</i>

00:14:06.210 --> 00:14:10.410
<i>The traitor's persistence 
beat out Katagiri Yuichi's wit.</i>

00:14:10.410 --> 00:14:11.870
<i>But what is this?</i>

00:14:12.240 --> 00:14:15.120
<i>Something in the image doesn't feel right...</i>

00:14:16.290 --> 00:14:17.680
Quick! Rewind the video!

00:14:17.680 --> 00:14:19.210
Huh? Okay.

00:14:22.420 --> 00:14:23.750
It can't be.

00:14:23.750 --> 00:14:25.670
Could this really have...

00:14:26.690 --> 00:14:31.650
We may have let a human 
abomination play the game.

00:14:32.140 --> 00:14:34.440
The game isn't over yet!

00:14:35.640 --> 00:14:36.680
Hey.

00:14:37.320 --> 00:14:39.490
I might have an idea.

00:14:39.940 --> 00:14:44.190
Sorry, Yuichi, but I have 
no interest in hearing you out.

00:14:44.190 --> 00:14:45.610
Even so...

00:14:45.990 --> 00:14:49.880
I just thought of a way to make
 the traitor expose themselves.

00:14:51.060 --> 00:14:52.890
Are you serious, Yuichi?

00:14:52.890 --> 00:14:55.200
Yeah. This time it'll totally work.

00:14:55.200 --> 00:14:59.670
Yuichi, are you going to talk crap 
and try to confuse us again?

00:14:59.670 --> 00:15:00.670
No way.

00:15:01.140 --> 00:15:04.810
Confused or not, even if we
 figure out who it is now,

00:15:04.810 --> 00:15:07.300
we can't stop Sawaragi 
from reaching the goal.

00:15:07.300 --> 00:15:09.330
W-Well, I guess you're right.

00:15:09.330 --> 00:15:13.510
But why would you want to 
figure out the traitor now, then?

00:15:13.510 --> 00:15:15.820
Well, that's because...

00:15:17.280 --> 00:15:20.440
You remember there's a penalty 
if you're caught lying, right?

00:15:20.600 --> 00:15:22.310
<b>- You may lie
 (if the lie is revealed, you'll be forced one space in front of the lead player)</b>

00:15:21.660 --> 00:15:27.150
And if you combine that with my earlier 
strategy to only bad-mouth yourself,

00:15:27.150 --> 00:15:32.030
everyone except the traitor will be 
able to go to the next game.

00:15:33.360 --> 00:15:34.480
Seriously?

00:15:35.870 --> 00:15:38.490
Everyone except the traitor 
reaches the goal?

00:15:38.490 --> 00:15:40.190
Can they really do that?

00:15:40.780 --> 00:15:44.090
This will be our last round 
of bad-mouthing, so...

00:15:43.670 --> 00:15:49.800
<b></b>Katagiri Yuichi

00:15:44.090 --> 00:15:46.940
We use these bad-mouth cards 
with names on them

00:15:44.580 --> 00:15:49.800
<b></b>Shibe Makoto

00:15:45.590 --> 00:15:49.800
<b></b>Kokorogi Yutori

00:15:46.590 --> 00:15:49.800
<b></b>Mikasa Tenji

00:15:46.940 --> 00:15:49.800
and all write the exact same thing.

00:15:47.630 --> 00:15:49.800
<b></b>Sawaragi Shiho

00:15:49.800 --> 00:15:51.490
The same thing?

00:15:51.490 --> 00:15:54.510
There's only one person it'll be true for—

00:15:55.010 --> 00:15:56.890
the traitor.

00:15:57.290 --> 00:15:59.390
Can a bad-mouth can do that?

00:15:59.390 --> 00:16:00.300
Sure, it can.

00:16:00.300 --> 00:16:02.310
Just write this on the bad-mouth card:

00:16:02.810 --> 00:16:06.820
"I'm the one who applied to 
play Tomodachi Game."

00:16:08.150 --> 00:16:11.020
I'm sure the traitor chose to play the game

00:16:11.020 --> 00:16:13.150
in order to destroy our friendship.

00:16:13.700 --> 00:16:17.080
Basically, the applicant 
must also be the traitor.

00:16:14.320 --> 00:16:17.080
<b>applicant =</b>

00:16:15.300 --> 00:16:17.080
<b>traitor</b>

00:16:17.080 --> 00:16:18.850
Y-You're right!

00:16:18.850 --> 00:16:22.210
So if we all write the same card 
with our names attached,

00:16:22.210 --> 00:16:27.890
the real traitor will actually have 
written the truth, and won't get a penalty.

00:16:27.890 --> 00:16:31.840
But the others will be penalized for lying.

00:16:28.590 --> 00:16:31.840
<b>Penalty</b>

00:16:28.590 --> 00:16:31.840
<b>Traitor</b>

00:16:28.590 --> 00:16:31.840
<b>No penalty</b>

00:16:32.260 --> 00:16:35.350
As a result, everyone except 
the traitor will be forced

00:16:35.350 --> 00:16:38.550
to the space after Sawaragi 
and will reach the goal.

00:16:38.550 --> 00:16:39.750
That makes sense!

00:16:39.750 --> 00:16:42.520
No wonder you waited until Shiho 
was right in front of the goal.

00:16:42.520 --> 00:16:46.500
B-But how are you going to prove
 the lie? If you can't—

00:16:46.500 --> 00:16:49.700
Not a problem. This way, 
we don't need to prove the lies.

00:16:49.700 --> 00:16:50.860
W-What?

00:16:50.860 --> 00:16:54.570
We're talking about whoever applied 
to play Tomodachi Game.

00:16:54.970 --> 00:16:57.100
Management obviously 
already knows who that is.

00:16:58.070 --> 00:17:00.050
Isn't that right, Manabu-sensei?

00:17:00.050 --> 00:17:02.080
Hmm. Yeah, I guess.

00:17:02.540 --> 00:17:05.520
If possible, I wanted us all 
to reach the goal together.

00:17:05.520 --> 00:17:08.420
But it's been such a mess 
so far, I figured it's better

00:17:08.420 --> 00:17:10.480
to leave the traitor in this game,

00:17:10.480 --> 00:17:12.460
and clear it without him.

00:17:12.900 --> 00:17:17.970
Then only true friends will be left 
to play the third game together.

00:17:19.100 --> 00:17:23.490
W-Wait! You can't guarantee 
everyone will write the same thing!

00:17:23.490 --> 00:17:26.310
If someone doesn't write it, 
we'll know he's the traitor.

00:17:26.310 --> 00:17:27.300
Huh?!

00:17:27.300 --> 00:17:31.520
If we keep going like this, Sawaragi 
will move on to the third game alone.

00:17:31.520 --> 00:17:34.430
Anyone okay with that is 
the just as bad as the traitor.

00:17:35.030 --> 00:17:35.940
Right, Shibe?

00:17:35.940 --> 00:17:38.550
Y-Yeah! I'll totally write it.

00:17:38.550 --> 00:17:39.950
Don't you agree, Tenji?

00:17:40.260 --> 00:17:43.080
You said you're on Sawaragi's 
side no matter what, right?

00:17:43.530 --> 00:17:45.500
O-Of course I am!

00:17:47.300 --> 00:17:50.630
All right. Why don't you go first, then?

00:17:51.010 --> 00:17:52.000
Huh?!

00:17:52.000 --> 00:17:55.130
Sawaragi trusts you more than anyone.

00:17:55.130 --> 00:17:58.340
Better to reassure her sooner 
rather than later, right?

00:17:58.340 --> 00:17:59.970
Tenji-san...

00:18:02.010 --> 00:18:03.640
<b></b>Mikasa Tenji

00:18:02.420 --> 00:18:03.640
Fine.

00:18:03.640 --> 00:18:06.230
<b></b>Mikasa Tenji

00:18:09.650 --> 00:18:12.240
<i>God damn it! I'm screwed!</i>

00:18:12.240 --> 00:18:14.280
<i>I never saw that coming!</i>

00:18:14.280 --> 00:18:18.440
<i>I'm out of time! There's gotta 
 be a way out of this!</i>

00:18:19.060 --> 00:18:20.160
<i>I know!</i>

00:18:20.560 --> 00:18:23.170
<i>I'll write the card like he said.</i>

00:18:23.170 --> 00:18:26.250
<i>When they figure out I'm the traitor, 
I'll feed them a conspiracy theory!</i>

00:18:26.780 --> 00:18:29.140
<i>I'll admit that I applied,</i>

00:18:29.140 --> 00:18:32.120
<i>and then say that someone else 
 blackmailed me into doing it.</i>

00:18:32.750 --> 00:18:36.120
<i>It'll take some effort, 
but it's already half-true.</i>

00:18:36.120 --> 00:18:39.260
<i>I can take my time figuring out 
a good excuse later.</i>

00:18:40.250 --> 00:18:41.180
I wrote it.

00:18:43.140 --> 00:18:44.850
Great! I'm up next.

00:18:44.850 --> 00:18:47.070
I'll do it <i>just</i> right.

00:18:47.070 --> 00:18:47.980
<i>What's with him?</i>

00:18:50.220 --> 00:18:54.820
Okay. You all wrote that you 
were the applicant, right?

00:18:56.070 --> 00:18:58.480
<i>Now it's just a matter of my acting.</i>

00:18:58.480 --> 00:19:00.660
<i>The instant they realize it was me,</i>

00:19:00.660 --> 00:19:02.280
<i>I'll start crying!</i>

00:19:02.280 --> 00:19:05.250
<i>I'll weep, cling to them, 
have a total breakdown...</i>

00:19:05.250 --> 00:19:10.040
<i>Yuichi's so dense, I'm sure 
he'll at least listen to me.</i>

00:19:10.470 --> 00:19:14.210
All right. Are you ready 
for the final round?

00:19:14.490 --> 00:19:18.210
Pay close attention. We should see 
something very interesting happen.

00:19:19.510 --> 00:19:20.740
Let's see.

00:19:20.740 --> 00:19:23.130
In total, this time there were...

00:19:23.130 --> 00:19:25.830
<i>There have to be five! Hurry it up!</i>

00:19:25.830 --> 00:19:27.720
<i>I can't hold back the tears!</i>

00:19:28.020 --> 00:19:32.020
What? There's just one. 
The rest are all blank.

00:19:32.020 --> 00:19:32.770
Huh?

00:19:32.770 --> 00:19:34.840
And it says, ahem,

00:19:34.840 --> 00:19:39.920
"I am the one who applied to play 
Tomodachi Game. —Mikasa Tenji"

00:19:38.300 --> 00:19:38.650
<b>Mi</b>

00:19:38.650 --> 00:19:39.050
<b>Mikasa</b>

00:19:39.050 --> 00:19:39.470
<b>Mikasa Ten</b>

00:19:39.470 --> 00:19:39.900
<b>Mikasa Tenji</b>

00:19:39.920 --> 00:19:41.450
W-Why...

00:19:41.450 --> 00:19:44.070
Why am I the only one who turned one in?!

00:19:47.290 --> 00:19:50.000
Tenji, didn't I tell you?

00:19:50.280 --> 00:19:54.120
"I thought of a way to make 
the traitor expose themself."

00:19:55.350 --> 00:19:58.130
E-Expose? No, I'm not...

00:19:59.200 --> 00:20:00.860
<i>Damn it!</i>

00:20:00.860 --> 00:20:02.850
<i>I have to cry to get their sympathy!</i>

00:20:02.850 --> 00:20:04.550
I-It's not like that...

00:20:06.150 --> 00:20:09.470
Will you just hear me out, please?!

00:20:11.780 --> 00:20:13.230
Don't cry, Tenji.

00:20:13.230 --> 00:20:15.230
<i>You really are dense!</i>

00:20:15.740 --> 00:20:16.360
Yui—

00:20:16.360 --> 00:20:19.190
You can make all the excuses you want later.

00:20:19.700 --> 00:20:23.220
But for now, you'd better spit it out.

00:20:24.150 --> 00:20:27.340
The truth was gonna come
 out sooner or later.

00:20:29.810 --> 00:20:33.210
Let's hear your answer 
to my question, Tenji.

00:20:33.210 --> 00:20:35.420
<i>W-What the hell is this?</i>

00:20:35.770 --> 00:20:38.540
<i>Is this the same Yuichi?!</i>

00:20:39.180 --> 00:20:43.370
Are you the one who applied 
to play the Tomodachi Game?

00:20:43.370 --> 00:20:45.920
<i>You're scaring the hell out of me!</i>

00:20:48.450 --> 00:20:50.390
Y-Yes.

00:20:50.990 --> 00:20:55.770
I applied to play the Tomodachi Game.

00:20:56.620 --> 00:20:58.290
What's going on?!

00:20:58.290 --> 00:21:02.400
Did Katagiri Yuichi realize that 
Mikasa Tenji was the traitor?

00:21:02.400 --> 00:21:06.380
If you rewatched from the start of 
second game, you'd understand, too.

00:21:06.380 --> 00:21:09.050
There were three clear abnormalities.

00:21:09.050 --> 00:21:11.880
You should be able to find three traps.

00:21:11.880 --> 00:21:13.750
Three traps?

00:21:13.750 --> 00:21:14.540
Yes.

00:21:14.540 --> 00:21:19.710
<b></b>Katagiri Yuichi

00:21:14.810 --> 00:21:20.300
And if you do, you'll understand 
how unique Katagiri Yuichi really is.

00:21:20.500 --> 00:21:22.920
<b>NEXT: I Really Can't Be Friends with a "Murderer"</b>
